Okay, evaluating the **Mercedes-Benz A-Class A35h**.

Similar to the A180h/A200h cases, Mercedes-Benz does not officially market a model named "A35h". However, the **most recent facelift of the Mercedes-AMG A35 (W177 generation)** introduced a **48V mild-hybrid (MHEV)** system as standard. This system adds a small electric boost via an integrated starter-generator (ISG) for improved efficiency and smoother power delivery, particularly at lower speeds and during start/stop.

Therefore, "A35h" almost certainly refers to the **current, facelifted Mercedes-AMG A35 4MATIC with the standard mild-hybrid system**. I will evaluate this specific model against today's (2024) market benchmarks, incorporating the effects of the MHEV system and other facelift updates.

